Z||000000||Ferrari_cdn||11-11-2001||11:10 PM||||about 5% of the time I try to shift into reverse, she wouldn't go in gear.  She would just stop before I can go in reverse.  I'll just move the shifter to neutral then try to jam in but wouldn't go all the way in.  I realized when I release the clutch a little, then she'll pop into reverse.  The other 95% of the time I don't have a problem shifting into reverse.  Whats up with that?  I'm stumped with this.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ferrari_cdn" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_cdn.JPG">   </A>  <BR>AIM: CanadianFiero<p>[This message has been edited by Ferrari_cdn (edited 11-11-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||avengador1||11-11-2001||11:19 PM||||Could be your sychros are worn or wearing out. Try to put it in first and rock the car then reverse. This happens every once in a while in mine with 159000 miles and that's what I do.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||11-12-2001||04:02 AM||||That's the idler gear... It's not lining up. You'll find that if you slap it into any gear, it will go smoothly into R. Nothing wrong. It's just the thing that prevents you from jamming it into reverse while moving. <P>Best fix is to slap it into gear. That will line things up. The idler isn't tapered as nicely as the rest of the "gears" (Crowns?)<P>I've noticed that some cars do it more than others... Doesn't seem to be representative of a problem. Just happens...<BR>||||reg||7
